,"restrictedSyntax","ts/no-empty-object-type","The `{}` (\"empty object\") type allows any non-nullish value, including literals like `0` and `\"\"`.\n- If that's what you want, disable this lint rule with an inline comment or configure the 'allowObjectTypes' rule option.\n- If you want a type meaning \"any object\", you probably want `object` instead.\n- If you want a type meaning \"any value\", you probably want `unknown` instead.","noEmptyObject",["14091","14092"],["14093"],["14094","14095"],["14096"],["14097","14098"],["14099"],["14100","14101"],["14102"],["14103"],["14104"],"node/prefer-global/process","Unexpected use of the global variable 'process'. Use 'require(\"process\")' instead.","preferModule",["14105"],["14106"],["14107"],["14108"],["14109"],["14110"],["14111"],["14112"],["14113"],"no-alert","Unexpected confirm.","unexpected",["14114"],["14115"],["14116"],"no-labels","Unexpected labeled statement.","unexpectedLabel",["14117"],"Unexpected label in continue statement.","unexpectedLabelInContinue",["14118"],"regexp/no-unused-capturing-group","Capturing group number 1 is defined but never used.","unusedCapturingGroup",["14119"],["14120"],"Capturing group number 2 is defined but never used.",["14121"],["14122"],"Capturing group number 3 is defined but never used.",["14123"],["14124"],"ts/ban-ts-comment","Do not use \"@ts-nocheck\" because it alters compilation errors.","tsDirectiveComment",["14125"],"no-useless-return","Unnecessary return statement.","unnecessaryReturn",["14126"],"regexp/no-super-linear-backtracking","The quantifier '\\s+' can exchange characters with '.*?'. Using any string accepted by /[\\t\\x0b\\f \\xa0\\u1680\\u2000-\\u200a\\u202f\\u205f\\u3000\\ufeff]+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking.","trade",["14127"],["14128"],["14129"],["14130"],["14131"],["14132"],["14133"],["14134"],["14135"],["14136"],["14137"],["14138"],["14139"],"antfu/no-top-level-await","Do not use top-level await","NoTopLevelAwait",["14140"],["14141"],["14142"],["14143"],["14144"],["14145"],["14146"],["14147"],["14148"],["14149"],["14150"],["14151"],["14152"],"ts/no-unnecessary-type-constraint","Constraining the generic type `Content` to `any` does nothing and is unnecessary.","unnecessaryConstraint",["14153"],["14154"],"jsdoc/check-param-names","Missing @param \"props.imageData\"",["14155"],"Missing @param \"props.cornerWidth\"",["14156"],"Missing @param \"props.pixelRatio\"",["14157"],"style/max-statements-per-line","This line has 2 statements. Maximum allowed is 1.","exceed","unused-imports/no-unused-vars","'e' is defined but never used.","unusedVar",["14158"],["14159"],["14160"],["14161"],["14162"],["14163"],["14164"],["14165"],["14166"],["14167"],["14168"],["14169"],["14170"],["14171"],["14172"],["14173"],["14174"],"ts/no-use-before-define","'handler' was used before it was defined.","noUseBeforeDefine","Constraining the generic type `TConfig` to `any` does nothing and is unnecessary.",["14175"],["14176"],"style/indent-binary-ops","Expected indentation of 0 spaces","wrongIndentation",{"range":"14177","text":"14178"},["14179"],"style/operator-linebreak","Bad line breaking before and after '?'.","badLinebreak",["14180"],["14181"],["14182"],"The quantifier '\\s*' can exchange characters with '[\\s\\S]*?'. Using any string accepted by /\\s+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking.",["14183"],["14184"],["14185"],["14186"],["14187"],["14188"],["14189"],["14190"],["14191"],["14192"],["14193"],["14194"],["14195"],["14196"],"no-extend-native","Object prototype is read only, properties should not be added.",["14197"],["14198"],"test/prefer-lowercase-title","`describe`s should begin with lowercase","lowerCaseTitle",{"range":"14199","text":"14200"},["14201"],"pnpm/yaml-no-unused-catalog-item","Catalog item \"vitest:vitest\" is not used in any package.json.","unusedCatalogItem",["14202"],["14203"],["14204"],["14205"],["14206"],["14207"],["14208"],["14209"],["14210"],["14211"],["14212"],"no-undef","'chrome' is not defined.","undef","'axCount' is assigned a value but never used. Allowed unused vars must match /^_/u.","Missing @param \"params.config\"","Missing @param \"params.executor\"","Missing @param \"params.input\"","Missing @param \"params.extensionBridge\"","Missing @param \"params.cdpBridge\"","Missing @param \"point.x\"","Missing @param \"point.y\"","The quantifier '\\s*' can exchange characters with '[^:\\n]+'. Using any string accepted by /[\\t\\x0b\\f\\r \\xa0\\u1680\\u2000-\\u200a\\u2028\\u2029\\u202f\\u205f\\u3000\\ufeff]+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking.",["14213"],"The quantifier '[^\\S\\r\\n]*' can exchange characters with '[\\s\\S]*?'. Using any string accepted by /[\\t\\x0b\\f \\xa0\\u1680\\u2000-\\u200a\\u2028\\u2029\\u202f\\u205f\\u3000\\ufeff]+/i, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking.",["14214"],"no-new-func","The Function constructor is eval.","noFunctionConstructor",["14215"],["14216"],"no-restricted-globals","Unexpected use of 'self'. Use `globalThis` instead.","customMessage",["14217"],["14218"],["14219"],["14220"],["14221"],["14222"],["14223"],["14224"],["14225"],["14226"],["14227"],["14228"],"The quantifier '\\s*' can exchange characters with '.*'. Using any string accepted by /\\s+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking.",["14229"],["14230"],["14231"],"'onCollect' was used before it was defined.",["14232"],"'onInterrupt' was used before it was defined.",["14233"],"The quantifier '(\"?)*' can exchange characters with '.*'. Using any string accepted by /.+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking. This is going to cause exponential backtracking resulting in exponential worst-case runtime behavior.",["14234"],"The quantifier '(\"?)*' can exchange characters with '\\s*'. Using any string accepted by /\\s+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking. This is going to cause exponential backtracking resulting in exponential worst-case runtime behavior.",["14235"],"This quantifier can reach itself via the loop '((\"?)*.*\\s*)*'. Using any string accepted by /[^]+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking. This is going to cause exponential backtracking resulting in exponential worst-case runtime behavior.","self",["14236"],"The quantifier '.*' can exchange characters with '(\"?)*'. Using any string accepted by /\"+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking. This is going to cause exponential backtracking resulting in exponential worst-case runtime behavior.",["14237"],"regexp/optimal-quantifier-concatenation","'(\"?)*' can be removed because it is already included by '.*'. This cannot be fixed automatically because it might change or remove a capturing group.","removeLeft",["14238"],"The quantifier '.*' can exchange characters with '\\s*'. Using any string accepted by /[\\t\\x0b\\f \\xa0\\u1680\\u2000-\\u200a\\u202f\\u205f\\u3000\\ufeff]+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking. This is going to cause exponential backtracking resulting in exponential worst-case runtime behavior.",{"range":"14239","text":"14240"},["14241"],"This quantifier can reach itself via the loop '((\"?)*.*\\s*)*'. Using any string accepted by /.+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking. This is going to cause exponential backtracking resulting in exponential worst-case runtime behavior.",["14242"],"The quantifier '\\s*' can exchange characters with '.*'. Using any string accepted by /[\\t\\x0b\\f \\xa0\\u1680\\u2000-\\u200a\\u202f\\u205f\\u3000\\ufeff]+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial backtracking. This is going to cause exponential backtracking resulting in exponential worst-case runtime behavior.",["14243"],"This quantifier can reach itself via the loop '((\"?)*.*\\s*)*'. Using any string accepted by /\\s+/, this can be exploited to cause at least polynomial b